   "reply": "Step 1 is done. I added `src/ledgerlite/money.py` with `parse(value: str | Decimal) -> Decimal`. I haven't run it or tested it, and I didn't touch `Ledger`.\n\n`parse` behaves like this:\n- **Wrong type:** anything other than `str` or `Decimal` raises `TypeError`. That includes `float` and `int`.\n- **Unparseable string:** raises `ValueError`.\n- **NaN or infinity:** raises `ValueError`. I added this check on top of your spec because `Decimal(\"NaN\") <= 0` raises `InvalidOperation` and infinity would pass the positive check.\n- **Zero or negative:** raises `ValueError(\"amount must be positive\")`, the same message `transfer` uses today.\n\n**Next step (step 2):** change `Ledger.transfer` in `src/ledgerlite/__init__.py` to call `money.parse(amount)`. That replaces the `Decimal(amount)` call and the manual `<= 0` check. `transfer` currently raises `decimal.InvalidOperation` on a malformed string, and after the change it will raise `ValueError`.\n\nI've stopped here, as you asked.",
